From 4d3627f5b27daef18a0141ecce8f3b8d1830f761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emergent-agent-e1 <github@emergent.sh>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:49:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(reports): use canonical private mileage aggregation
 (AVL16 + cutover)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Aligns the Swiss fiscal/monthly report (/reports/tax-swiss) private km with the SAME
source as km-summary (no 2nd AVL16 logic):
- private_mileage.aggregate_private_km_for_scope(): multi-vehicle wrapper reusing the
  per-vehicle aggregate_private_km; fleet source AVL16|GPS_FALLBACK|MIXED_TRANSITION|
  UNAVAILABLE; null!=0.
- reports.py tax-swiss: perso_km + pct_perso/pct_pro/total_km via the aggregator over the
  vehicles in the scoped trips; pro_km unchanged; private_km_source kept for audit.
Flag PRIVATE_KM_SOURCE_AVL16 default OFF => reports keep legacy GPS numbers (no prod change).
Tests: +5 report-alignment (flag OFF==legacy, post-cutover AVL16/UNAVAILABLE, crossing=MIXED,
pct_perso from AVL16). Full regression 123/123 PASS. Verified by testing_agent.

Note: weekly driver report endpoint does not exist yet (documented); CSV/XLSX/PDF per-trip
exports keep trip rows (location redacted) — km totals coherence handled via aggregator.
